  "chapter": {
    "number": 69,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(70) For the end, by David for a remembrance, that the Lord may save me."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Draw near, O God, to my help.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let them be ashamed and confounded that seek my soul: let them be turned backward and put to shame, that wish me evil.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let them that say to me, Aha, aha, be turned back and put to shame immediately.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let all that seek you exult and be glad in you: and let those that love your salvation say continually, Let God be magnified.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But I am poor and needy; O God, help me: you are my helper and deliverer, O Lord, delay not.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": []
  },
